KG42.register("nodes-b5dbc4ad55d49ea8acc6533e",{"id":"COMP-c19b72437a1d5a78","code":"PRC042","label":"Electricity-clearing prices and hydrogen reference-price spreads","definition":"The electricity unit price is formed by iterative clearing; when the supply and demand curves do not intersect, the price of the last accepted unit on the curve that has a surplus is taken, and λ_t^{DP}≤λ_t^{L}≤λ_t^{DS} is satisfied. The hydrogen unit price is separately formed as λ_t^{HL}=λ_t^{HS}−μ^H and is controlled by the sole hydrogen producer, HSSA.","layer":"L6","template_code":"DA","concept_id":"pricing.local","concept_ids":["pricing.local"],"identity_dimensions":{"identity_fields":["Object: unit transaction prices of local electricity and hydrogen","Electricity-price relation: the clearing acceptance result forms the unit price; when the curves do not intersect, the price of the last accepted unit on the surplus side is used","Hydrogen-price relation: hydrogen-station reference price minus a price-spread parameter","Output: λ_t^{L} (€/kWh) and λ_t^{HL} (€/kg)"]},"exclusions":["The lower and upper bounds of the electricity price are the DisCo purchase price and the electricity selling price, respectively","Distinguishes the current-round electricity price without HSSA, λ_t^{LnA,(r)}, the previous-round electricity price, and the previous-round hydrogen price","The hydrogen-price reference is λ_t^{HS}; μ^H is a price-spread parameter, and no fixed numerical value is specified","When μ^H>0, HV purchases according to demand and available quantity; the source describes HSSA as tending to select a positive price spread close to zero","Prices may be used for bid formation, participation judgment, and quantity response; each use is retained separately"],"members":[{"id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","market_meaning":"Local clearing results provide feedback for players to adapt their demand-bid parameters toward maximizing their own utilities. Scope: Demand-bid parameter updates during iterative LEM clearing. Condition: A player updates its demand bid using the preceding cleared results. A completed LEM clearing precedes the subsequent demand-bid parameter adjustment. Scope: Temporal order of demand-bid updates between successive LEM clearings. Condition: An additional bid adjustment is undertaken during the iterative process. On the second segment of a Load's demand-bid schedule, the preceding local clearing price supplies the submitted bidding price. Scope: Load demand-bid schedule in equation (33), using the preceding iteration's LEM electricity price. Condition: The requested quantity belongs to S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)}, the closed interval from scenario-average Load demand in iteration r minus its accepted amount in iteration r-1 through scenario-average Load demand in iteration r. On the second segment of an HV's hydrogen demand-bid schedule, the preceding local hydrogen price supplies the submitted bidding price. Scope: HV hydrogen demand-bid schedule in equation (34), using the preceding iteration's LEM hydrogen price. Condition: The requested quantity belongs to S_{k,t}^{HV2,(r)}, the closed interval from scenario-average total hydrogen purchases in iteration r minus hydrogen purchased in the LEM in iteration r-1 through scenario-average total hydrogen purchases in iteration r. The HSSA uses the LEM price cleared without its participation as the price of its subsequently generated electricity demand bid. Scope: HSSA electricity demand-bid formation after the LEM clearing without the HSSA in the same iteration. Condition: The HSSA's requested electricity quantity lies in the closed interval [0, P_t^{ALP,(r)}] specified in equation (36). A Load reduces its bidding price to seek higher utility when the specified allocation conditions hold; otherwise this adjustment is not made. Scope: Load demand-bid price revision for resubmission during Step 3 of the iterative clearing procedure. Condition: The Load's own bidding amount is fully accepted and positive, while total accepted supply is less than total offered supply, as specified in equations (47)-(48). The electricity-price rise precedes the HSSA's possible reduction of its bidding amount; the reduction is not mandatory. Scope: The HSSA's optional electricity-demand quantity response during iterative supply-demand balancing. Condition: A supplier's offer is completely accepted while some consumer bidding amount remains, the electricity price consequently rises, and the HSSA chooses the described demand-reduction response. Demand submissions communicate bids in price and amount in place of players' preferences and detailed appliance profiles. Scope: Information communicated through participating players' demand bids. Demand-bid parameters should assure the submitting player higher utility in the LEM than in trading with the DisCo/HS. Scope: Demand-bid parameter selection by players choosing to participate in the LEM. Condition: A player elects to submit a demand bid in the LEM rather than rely on trading with the DisCo/HS. Players must ensure that their adjustments introduce no decrease in their own utilities. Scope: Demand-bid adjustments during the iterative LEM procedure. Condition: A participating player adjusts its demand bid. The adjustment in iteration r is to revise the adjustment made in iteration r-1. Scope: Loads' demand-bid adjustments in Step 3, comparing iterations r-1 and r. Condition: The preceding adjustment brings no increase in the Load's utility. The first segment of the Load demand-bid schedule assigns the DisCo electricity selling price as the bidding price. Scope: First segment of the Load electricity demand-bid schedule in equation (33). Condition: The requested quantity belongs to S_{j,t}^{Load1,(r)}, the closed interval from zero through scenario-average Load demand in iteration r minus its accepted amount in iteration r-1. The first segment of the HV hydrogen demand-bid schedule assigns the hydrogen-station price as the bidding price. Scope: First segment of the HV hydrogen demand-bid schedule in equation (34). Condition: The requested quantity belongs to S_{k,t}^{HV1,(r)}, the closed interval from zero through scenario-average total hydrogen purchases in iteration r minus hydrogen purchased in the LEM in iteration r-1.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Demand-bid adjustments during the iterative LEM procedure. | Demand-bid parameter selection by players choosing to participate in the LEM. | Demand-bid parameter updates during iterative LEM clearing. | First segment of the HV hydrogen demand-bid schedule in equation (34). | First segment of the Load electricity demand-bid schedule in equation (33). | HSSA electricity demand-bid formation after the LEM clearing without the HSSA in the same iteration. | HV hydrogen demand-bid schedule in equation (34), using the preceding iteration's LEM hydrogen price. | Information communicated through participating players' demand bids. | Load demand-bid price revision for resubmission during Step 3 of the iterative clearing procedure. | Load demand-bid schedule in equation (33), using the preceding iteration's LEM electricity price. | Loads' demand-bid adjustments in Step 3, comparing iterations r-1 and r. | Temporal order of demand-bid updates between successive LEM clearings. | The HSSA's optional electricity-demand quantity response during iterative supply-demand balancing.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e25"]},"constraint_refs":["47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C003","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C004","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C005","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C007"],"decision_anchor":"bidding.demand","source_rule_sha256":"1647f86538d700837059c307789c7e879d669252d17d688720909513da383d62","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","market_meaning":"Cleared LEM results provide information used by players to update their offering parameters. Scope: Players' supply-offer updates between iterations of LEM clearing. Condition: Players adjust their offering parameters following a clearing result. LEM clearing precedes the players' subsequent offering-parameter updates. Scope: Post-clearing offering-parameter updates in the iterative procedure; initial submissions are outside this temporal assertion. The HSSA uses the LEM electricity price cleared without the HSSA to generate its supply-offer parameters. Scope: HSSA electricity supply-offer generation between the clearing without HSSA and the clearing with HSSA in an iteration. Condition: The current iteration has produced a cleared LEM price without the HSSA. The resulting rise in the LEM electricity price can be followed by an HSSA response that increases its offered quantity; this response is possible rather than mandatory. Scope: HSSA electricity offered-quantity response in the described surplus-demand adjustment during iterative clearing. Condition: A supplier's offering amount is completely accepted while consumers still have unaccepted bidding quantities; the supplier elevates its offering price and the LEM electricity price rises. Supply-offer parameters should assure the submitting player higher utility in the LEM than in trading with the DisCo/HS. Scope: Supply-offer parameters of players that can choose between LEM participation and trading with the DisCo/HS. Players must ensure that their supply-offer adjustments introduce no decrease in their own utilities. Scope: Players' supply-offer adjustments during the iterative LEM procedure. Condition: A player adjusts its supply offer. Players broadcast their offers instead of their preferences and detailed utilization profiles, while competing on both price and amount. Scope: Information disclosed through supply submissions in the distribution-level LEM.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"HSSA electricity offered-quantity response in the described surplus-demand adjustment during iterative clearing. | HSSA electricity supply-offer generation between the clearing without HSSA and the clearing with HSSA in an iteration. | Information disclosed through supply submissions in the distribution-level LEM. | Players' supply-offer adjustments during the iterative LEM procedure. | Players' supply-offer updates between iterations of LEM clearing. | Post-clearing offering-parameter updates in the iterative procedure; initial submissions are outside this temporal assertion. | Supply-offer parameters of players that can choose between LEM participation and trading with the DisCo/HS.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e25"]},"constraint_refs":["47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C003","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C004","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C008","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C009"],"decision_anchor":"bidding.supply","source_rule_sha256":"d8cd244edae596c208b49132740df1d7feccf0f2fc85f104d0bec3a6f1cc9a66","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R003::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","market_meaning":"Load demand submissions provide inputs to the first electricity clearing. Scope: Electricity clearing using Load submissions in the first phase of each iteration. Condition: The HSSA is absent from this clearing phase. DG supply submissions provide inputs to the first electricity clearing. Scope: Electricity clearing using DG submissions in the first phase of each iteration. Condition: The HSSA is absent from this clearing phase. Load and HSSA demand submissions provide inputs to the electricity clearing with the HSSA. Scope: Electricity clearing using Load and HSSA demand submissions in the second phase of each iteration. Condition: The HSSA is present in this clearing phase. DG and HSSA supply submissions provide inputs to the electricity clearing with the HSSA. Scope: Electricity clearing using DG and HSSA supply submissions in the second phase of each iteration. Condition: The HSSA is present in this clearing phase. Each Load's submitted bidding quantity bounds its accepted electricity allocation above; the written feasible interval also specifies a strictly positive accepted quantity. Scope: Modeled Load electricity allocations in clearing both without and with the HSSA, using constraint (40). Each DG's submitted offering quantity bounds its accepted electricity allocation above; the written feasible interval also specifies a strictly positive accepted quantity. Scope: Modeled DG electricity allocations in clearing both without and with the HSSA, using constraint (39). The HSSA's submitted bidding quantity bounds its accepted electricity demand above; the written feasible interval also specifies a strictly positive accepted quantity. Scope: The HSSA's accepted electricity demand in the clearing model with the HSSA, constraint (44). Condition: The clearing phase includes the HSSA. The HSSA's submitted offering quantity bounds its accepted electricity supply above; the written feasible interval also specifies a strictly positive accepted quantity. Scope: The HSSA's accepted electricity supply in the clearing model with the HSSA, constraint (43). Condition: The clearing phase includes the HSSA. The LEM operator performs local market clearing. Scope: Market clearing in each iteration of the proposed LEM procedure. Control of the local hydrogen price enables the HSSA to determine the quantity of hydrogen traded in the LEM. Scope: Determination of the quantity of hydrogen traded in the LEM through the hydrogen price under equation (31). Condition: The HSSA is the unique hydrogen producer in the LEM. The LEM clearing method should respect the merit order principle in every iteration. Scope: Each iteration of the proposed LEM clearing procedure. Electricity clearing without the HSSA occurs first, followed by electricity clearing with the HSSA. Scope: The two electricity-clearing phases within each iteration. Total accepted DG electricity supply must equal total accepted Load electricity demand. Scope: Electricity allocations in the clearing model without the HSSA, constraint (38). Condition: The HSSA is absent from this clearing phase. Total accepted DG supply plus accepted HSSA supply must equal total accepted Load demand plus accepted HSSA demand. Scope: Electricity allocations in the clearing model with the HSSA, constraint (42). Condition: The HSSA is present in this clearing phase. The procedure returns to Step 1 to repeat the clearing process. Scope: The continuation decision at Step 4 of the iterative clearing procedure. Condition: Further offering/bidding adjustment is still needed. The iteration terminates and final LEM clearing is performed in the presence of the HSSA. Scope: The termination decision at Step 4 of the iterative clearing procedure. Condition: No further offering/bidding adjustment is needed.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Determination of the quantity of hydrogen traded in the LEM through the hydrogen price under equation (31). | Each iteration of the proposed LEM clearing procedure. | Electricity allocations in the clearing model with the HSSA, constraint (42). | Electricity allocations in the clearing model without the HSSA, constraint (38). | Electricity clearing using DG and HSSA supply submissions in the second phase of each iteration. | Electricity clearing using DG submissions in the first phase of each iteration. | Electricity clearing using Load and HSSA demand submissions in the second phase of each iteration. | Electricity clearing using Load submissions in the first phase of each iteration. | Market clearing in each iteration of the proposed LEM procedure. | Modeled DG electricity allocations in clearing both without and with the HSSA, using constraint (39). | Modeled Load electricity allocations in clearing both without and with the HSSA, using constraint (40). | The HSSA's accepted electricity demand in the clearing model with the HSSA, constraint (44). | The HSSA's accepted electricity supply in the clearing model with the HSSA, constraint (43). | The continuation decision at Step 4 of the iterative clearing procedure. | The termination decision at Step 4 of the iterative clearing procedure. | The two electricity-clearing phases within each iteration.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e25"]},"constraint_refs":["47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C010"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"5b4eabcb513b4c8b4405936cab8e94ecc7682875ab559a420d762be3ea642db5","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R003","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R007::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","market_meaning":"Load participation is conditional on the iteration's local electricity price being strictly lower than the DisCo selling price. Scope: Electricity LEM; Load participation in iteration r-1 at time slot t. Condition: The LEM electricity price satisfies λ_t^{L,(r-1)} \u003c λ_t^{DS}, the DisCo selling price. Household Loads may choose portfolios of electricity purchases from the DisCo and the LEM according to their own utility function. Scope: Household Loads; electricity purchasing options. HVs may purchase hydrogen from the HS or in the LEM. Scope: HVs; hydrogen purchasing options. The HSSA may purchase electricity from both the DisCo and the LEM. Scope: The HSSA acting as an electricity buyer.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Electricity LEM; Load participation in iteration r-1 at time slot t. | HVs; hydrogen purchasing options. | Household Loads; electricity purchasing options. | The HSSA acting as an electricity buyer.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g02-e12"]},"constraint_refs":["47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C001"],"decision_anchor":"participation.consumer","source_rule_sha256":"126f03a096cf9aa980dfb45675b7a6467e8ee97c8c740351ef5cac9f63387d22","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R007","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","market_meaning":"Submission of electricity offers is a means of LEM participation for renewable DGs and the supplier-capable HSS/HSSA. Scope: Electricity-supply participation of renewable DGs and the HSS/HSSA in the LEM. Submission of an electricity bid is a means of LEM participation for the HSS/HSSA when purchasing electricity. Scope: Electricity-demand submissions by the supplier-capable HSS/HSSA. Condition: The HSSA participates as an electricity buyer. Preliminary local clearing without the HSSA, generating its cleared electricity price, precedes participation of the supplier-capable HSSA in that iteration. Scope: HSS/HSSA participation within iteration r of the proposed LEM procedure. A renewable DG's participation in the r-1th LEM iteration is conditional on the local electricity price exceeding the DisCo purchasing price paid to the DG. Scope: Renewable-DG electricity participation at time t in the r-1th LEM iteration. Condition: \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} > \\lambda_t^{DP}. Supplier-capable players share the stated permission to choose LEM participation or trade with their applicable DisCo/HS alternative. Scope: Venue choice stated for all LEM players, including renewable DGs and the supplier-capable HSS. The HSSA may sell both electricity and hydrogen in the LEM. Scope: HSSA participation as an electricity and hydrogen supplier in the LEM.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Electricity-demand submissions by the supplier-capable HSS/HSSA. | Electricity-supply participation of renewable DGs and the HSS/HSSA in the LEM. | HSS/HSSA participation within iteration r of the proposed LEM procedure. | HSSA participation as an electricity and hydrogen supplier in the LEM. | Renewable-DG electricity participation at time t in the r-1th LEM iteration. | Venue choice stated for all LEM players, including renewable DGs and the supplier-capable HSS.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E02b","v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g03-e001"]},"constraint_refs":["47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C004"],"decision_anchor":"participation.prosumer","source_rule_sha256":"18a906a32f4c2438a6bf4e922baf40311c5a96b1e2b164c9a0d8fd63e7eb3580","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R008","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R009","market_meaning":"The iterative local market clearing process generates electricity prices to balance supply and demand. Scope: Electricity-price formation through iterative LEM clearing. The last accepted unit of the local allocation on the surplus curve supplies the unit price used as the LEM price. Scope: Electricity pricing from accepted local allocations when supply and demand curves do not intersect. Condition: The supply and demand curves fail to intersect. The LEM electricity price is bounded by the DisCo purchasing and selling electricity prices. Scope: Electricity-price bounds in the LEM. The LEM hydrogen price equals the hydrogen-station price minus the parameter µ^H, as specified by equation (31). Scope: Hydrogen pricing in the LEM.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Electricity pricing from accepted local allocations when supply and demand curves do not intersect. | Electricity-price bounds in the LEM. | Electricity-price formation through iterative LEM clearing. | Hydrogen pricing in the LEM.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g02-e08","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e24"]},"constraint_refs":["47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C001","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C002","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C003","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C004"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"c63c718d5941d7d21130f6f592c9076ed9222e70494af459761a112631c3b90c","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":true}],"paper_ids":["47-electricity_hydrogen_market"],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":", p y 24) P i,tDGdeal,(r−1) at the price of λL,(r−1)t in the r −1th iteration, then the offering par","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{DS} \\text{ if } P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} \\in S_{j,t}^{Load1,(r)}; \\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} \\text{ if } P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} \\in S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)} (33) where S_{j,t}^{Load1,(r)} = [0, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)} - P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r-1)}], S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)} = [\\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)} - P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r-1)}, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)}]. Also note that \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} \u003c \\lambda_t^{DS}, otherwise the Load would not participate in the r-1th iteration of LEM.","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"\\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{DS} \\text{ if } P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} \\in S_{j,t}^{Load1,(r)}; \\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} \\text{ if } P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} \\in S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)} (33) where S_{j,t}^{Load1,(r)} = [0, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)} - P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r-1)}], S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)} = [\\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)} - P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r-1)}, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)}]. Also note that \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} \u003c \\lambda_t^{DS}, otherwise the Load would not participate in the r-1th iteration of LEM."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e13","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p05-c2r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"(33) ro- P j,t,sL oad,(r ) −P j,tL oaddeal,(r −1) ],SLj,toad2,(r ) where SLj,toad1,(r ) =[0, N1sThe ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\lambda_{k,t}^{HVbid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{HS} \\text{ if } Q_{k,t}^{HVbid,(r)} \\in S_{k,t}^{HV1,(r)}; \\lambda_{k,t}^{HVbid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{HL,(r-1)} \\text{ if } Q_{k,t}^{HVbid,(r)} \\in S_{k,t}^{HV2,(r)} (34) where S_{k,t}^{HV1,(r)} = [0, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s Q_{k,t,s}^{HVP,(r)} - Q_{k,t}^{HVL,(r-1)}], S_{k,t}^{HV2,(r)} = [\\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s Q_{k,t,s}^{HVP,(r)} - Q_{k,t}^{HVL,(r-1)}, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s Q_{k,t,s}^{HVP,(r)}].","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"\\lambda_{k,t}^{HVbid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{HS} \\text{ if } Q_{k,t}^{HVbid,(r)} \\in S_{k,t}^{HV1,(r)}; \\lambda_{k,t}^{HVbid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{HL,(r-1)} \\text{ if } Q_{k,t}^{HVbid,(r)} \\in S_{k,t}^{HV2,(r)} (34) where S_{k,t}^{HV1,(r)} = [0, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s Q_{k,t,s}^{HVP,(r)} - Q_{k,t}^{HVL,(r-1)}], S_{k,t}^{HV2,(r)} = [\\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s Q_{k,t,s}^{HVP,(r)} - Q_{k,t}^{HVL,(r-1)}, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s Q_{k,t,s}^{HVP,(r)}]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e14","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p06-c1r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"XIAO et al.: LOCAL ENERGY MARKET FOR ELECTRICITY AND HYDROGEN According to the iterative clearing me","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"According to the iterative clearing method, which will be described in Section IV-C, the HSSA only participates in the LEM after the LEM is cleared in the absence of the HSSA with \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)} generated. Therefore, the offering/bidding parameters of the HSSA are \\lambda_t^{Aoffer,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)}, if P_t^{Aoffer,(r)} \\in [0, P_t^{ALS,(r)}] (35); \\lambda_t^{Abid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)}, if P_t^{Abid,(r)} \\in [0, P_t^{ALP,(r)}] (36).","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"According to the iterative clearing method, which will be described in Section IV-C, the HSSA only participates in the LEM after the LEM is cleared in the absence of the HSSA with \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)} generated. Therefore, the offering/bidding parameters of the HSSA are \\lambda_t^{Aoffer,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)}, if P_t^{Aoffer,(r)} \\in [0, P_t^{ALS,(r)}] (35); \\lambda_t^{Abid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)}, if P_t^{Abid,(r)} \\in [0, P_t^{ALP,(r)}] (36)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e16","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"DGs and Loads are zero, the offering/bidding parameters of each DG and Load are acquired based on th","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Step 1: Assume the amounts of electricity accepted by all DGs and Loads are zero, the offering/bidding parameters of each DG and Load are acquired based on the optimization of utility functions. The LEM is firstly cleared in the absence of the HSSA after receiving all offering/bidding parameters from DGs and Loads, because the HSSA will use the cleared LEM price without HSSA to generate offering/bidding parameters, according to (35) and (36). The mathematical models of LEM clearing in the absence of the HSSA are as follows, and the objective is to achieve the maximum value of social welfare, represented as \\max_{\\Gamma^{LM,(r)}} U^{LM,(r)} = \\sum_j \\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r)} - \\sum_i \\lambda_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r)} (37) s.t. \\sum_i P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r)} = \\sum_j P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r)} (38); 0 \u003c P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r)} \\le P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} (39); 0 \u003c P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r)} \\le P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} (40).","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"Step 1: Assume the amounts of electricity accepted by all DGs and Loads are zero, the offering/bidding parameters of each DG and Load are acquired based on the optimization of utility functions. The LEM is firstly cleared in the absence of the HSSA after receiving all offering/bidding parameters from DGs and Loads, because the HSSA will use the cleared LEM price without HSSA to generate offering/bidding parameters, according to (35) and (36). The mathematical models of LEM clearing in the absence of the HSSA are as follows, and the objective is to achieve the maximum value of social welfare, represented as \\max_{\\Gamma^{LM,(r)}} U^{LM,(r)} = \\sum_j \\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r)} - \\sum_i \\lambda_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r)} (37) s.t. \\sum_i P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r)} = \\sum_j P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r)} (38); 0 \u003c P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r)} \\le P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} (39); 0 \u003c P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r)} \\le P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} (40)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON POWER SYSTEMS, VOL. 33, NO. 4, JULY 2018 r), In contrast, the electricity price","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In contrast, the electricity prices are formed through an iteration process to balance supply and demand. As stated in the Step. 3 of the algorithm, the sequences of proposed bids for each consumer j generated by the algorithm are increasing, while the sequences of proposed offers for each producer i are decreasing. To be specific, in a time slot when the supplier finds out its offering amount is completely accepted, whereas there is still some bidding amount of the consumers left, the supplier will elevate its offering price intending to achieve higher utility. In this case, the price will rise consequently, and then the HSSA may increase its offering amount or reduce its bidding amount. As a result, the total supply increases or the total demand decreases, until the supplier no longer observes the complete acceptance of its offering amount or an increase in its utility. It is similar for the case when the consumer observes its bidding amount is completely accepted, whereas there is still some offering amount of the suppliers left. Moreover, as stated in Section IV-A, in the case where the supply and demand curves fail to intersect, the LEM price will be settled as the price of the last unit of accepted amount of the curve that has a surplus. Therefore, the price varies during the iteration process to balance the supply and demand, and will necessarily converge.","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","quote":"In contrast, the electricity prices are formed through an iteration process to balance supply and demand. As stated in the Step. 3 of the algorithm, the sequences of proposed bids for each consumer j generated by the algorithm are increasing, while the sequences of proposed offers for each producer i are decreasing. To be specific, in a time slot when the supplier finds out its offering amount is completely accepted, whereas there is still some bidding amount of the consumers left, the supplier will elevate its offering price intending to achieve higher utility. In this case, the price will rise consequently, and then the HSSA may increase its offering amount or reduce its bidding amount. As a result, the total supply increases or the total demand decreases, until the supplier no longer observes the complete acceptance of its offering amount or an increase in its utility. It is similar for the case when the consumer observes its bidding amount is completely accepted, whereas there is still some offering amount of the suppliers left. Moreover, as stated in Section IV-A, in the case where the supply and demand curves fail to intersect, the LEM price will be settled as the price of the last unit of accepted amount of the curve that has a surplus. Therefore, the price varies during the iteration process to balance the supply and demand, and will necessarily converge."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e16","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"DGs and Loads are zero, the offering/bidding parameters of each DG and Load are acquired based on th","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Step 1: Assume the amounts of electricity accepted by all DGs and Loads are zero, the offering/bidding parameters of each DG and Load are acquired based on the optimization of utility functions. The LEM is firstly cleared in the absence of the HSSA after receiving all offering/bidding parameters from DGs and Loads, because the HSSA will use the cleared LEM price without HSSA to generate offering/bidding parameters, according to (35) and (36). The mathematical models of LEM clearing in the absence of the HSSA are as follows, and the objective is to achieve the maximum value of social welfare, represented as \\max_{\\Gamma^{LM,(r)}} U^{LM,(r)} = \\sum_j \\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r)} - \\sum_i \\lambda_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r)} (37) s.t. \\sum_i P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r)} = \\sum_j P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r)} (38); 0 \u003c P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r)} \\le P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} (39); 0 \u003c P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r)} \\le P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} (40).","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","quote":"Step 1: Assume the amounts of electricity accepted by all DGs and Loads are zero, the offering/bidding parameters of each DG and Load are acquired based on the optimization of utility functions. The LEM is firstly cleared in the absence of the HSSA after receiving all offering/bidding parameters from DGs and Loads, because the HSSA will use the cleared LEM price without HSSA to generate offering/bidding parameters, according to (35) and (36). The mathematical models of LEM clearing in the absence of the HSSA are as follows, and the objective is to achieve the maximum value of social welfare, represented as \\max_{\\Gamma^{LM,(r)}} U^{LM,(r)} = \\sum_j \\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r)} - \\sum_i \\lambda_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r)} (37) s.t. \\sum_i P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r)} = \\sum_j P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r)} (38); 0 \u003c P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r)} \\le P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} (39); 0 \u003c P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r)} \\le P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} (40)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON POWER SYSTEMS, VOL. 33, NO. 4, JULY 2018 r), In contrast, the electricity price","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In contrast, the electricity prices are formed through an iteration process to balance supply and demand. As stated in the Step. 3 of the algorithm, the sequences of proposed bids for each consumer j generated by the algorithm are increasing, while the sequences of proposed offers for each producer i are decreasing. To be specific, in a time slot when the supplier finds out its offering amount is completely accepted, whereas there is still some bidding amount of the consumers left, the supplier will elevate its offering price intending to achieve higher utility. In this case, the price will rise consequently, and then the HSSA may increase its offering amount or reduce its bidding amount. As a result, the total supply increases or the total demand decreases, until the supplier no longer observes the complete acceptance of its offering amount or an increase in its utility. It is similar for the case when the consumer observes its bidding amount is completely accepted, whereas there is still some offering amount of the suppliers left. Moreover, as stated in Section IV-A, in the case where the supply and demand curves fail to intersect, the LEM price will be settled as the price of the last unit of accepted amount of the curve that has a surplus. Therefore, the price varies during the iteration process to balance the supply and demand, and will necessarily converge.","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","quote":"In contrast, the electricity prices are formed through an iteration process to balance supply and demand. As stated in the Step. 3 of the algorithm, the sequences of proposed bids for each consumer j generated by the algorithm are increasing, while the sequences of proposed offers for each producer i are decreasing. To be specific, in a time slot when the supplier finds out its offering amount is completely accepted, whereas there is still some bidding amount of the consumers left, the supplier will elevate its offering price intending to achieve higher utility. In this case, the price will rise consequently, and then the HSSA may increase its offering amount or reduce its bidding amount. As a result, the total supply increases or the total demand decreases, until the supplier no longer observes the complete acceptance of its offering amount or an increase in its utility. It is similar for the case when the consumer observes its bidding amount is completely accepted, whereas there is still some offering amount of the suppliers left. Moreover, as stated in Section IV-A, in the case where the supply and demand curves fail to intersect, the LEM price will be settled as the price of the last unit of accepted amount of the curve that has a surplus. Therefore, the price varies during the iteration process to balance the supply and demand, and will necessarily converge."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":", p y 24) P i,tDGdeal,(r−1) at the price of λL,(r−1)t in the r −1th iteration, then the offering par","equation_id":"(32)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For DG i, if the accepted amount of electricity in the LEM is P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r-1)} at the price of \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} in the r-1th iteration, then the offering parameters in the tth iteration are \\lambda_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} = \\begin{cases} \\lambda_t^{DP}, & \\text{if } P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} \\in S_{i,t}^{DG1,(r)} \\\\ \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)}, & \\text{if } P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} \\in S_{i,t}^{DG2,(r)} \\end{cases} \\quad (32) where S_{i,t}^{DG1,(r)} = [0, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{i,t,s}^{DG} - P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r-1)}], S_{i,t}^{DG2,(r)} = [\\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{i,t,s}^{DG} - P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r-1)}, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{i,t,s}^{DG}]. Note that \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} > \\lambda_t^{DP}, otherwise the DG would not participate in the r-1th iteration of LEM.","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","quote":"For DG i, if the accepted amount of electricity in the LEM is P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r-1)} at the price of \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} in the r-1th iteration, then the offering parameters in the tth iteration are \\lambda_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} = \\begin{cases} \\lambda_t^{DP}, & \\text{if } P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} \\in S_{i,t}^{DG1,(r)} \\\\ \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)}, & \\text{if } P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} \\in S_{i,t}^{DG2,(r)} \\end{cases} \\quad (32) where S_{i,t}^{DG1,(r)} = [0, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{i,t,s}^{DG} - P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r-1)}], S_{i,t}^{DG2,(r)} = [\\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{i,t,s}^{DG} - P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r-1)}, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{i,t,s}^{DG}]. Note that \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} > \\lambda_t^{DP}, otherwise the DG would not participate in the r-1th iteration of LEM."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e14","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p06-c1r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"XIAO et al.: LOCAL ENERGY MARKET FOR ELECTRICITY AND HYDROGEN According to the iterative clearing me","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"According to the iterative clearing method, which will be described in Section IV-C, the HSSA only participates in the LEM after the LEM is cleared in the absence of the HSSA with \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)} generated. Therefore, the offering/bidding parameters of the HSSA are \\lambda_t^{Aoffer,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)}, if P_t^{Aoffer,(r)} \\in [0, P_t^{ALS,(r)}] (35); \\lambda_t^{Abid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)}, if P_t^{Abid,(r)} \\in [0, P_t^{ALP,(r)}] (36).","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","quote":"According to the iterative clearing method, which will be described in Section IV-C, the HSSA only participates in the LEM after the LEM is cleared in the absence of the HSSA with \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)} generated. Therefore, the offering/bidding parameters of the HSSA are \\lambda_t^{Aoffer,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)}, if P_t^{Aoffer,(r)} \\in [0, P_t^{ALS,(r)}] (35); \\lambda_t^{Abid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)}, if P_t^{Abid,(r)} \\in [0, P_t^{ALP,(r)}] (36)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e15","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"C. The Iterative Clearing Procedure The HVs are the only consumers of hydrogen in the LEM, and their","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The HVs are the only consumers of hydrogen in the LEM, and their trading strategies are quite easy to capture. According to (13)-(20) and (34), the HVs will purchase hydrogen from the LEM as much as they need or the LEM can supply, as long as the hydrogen price in the LEM is lower than that from the HS (\\mu^H > 0 in (31)). Since the HSSA is the unique hydrogen producer in the LEM, it is capable of settling the traded amount of hydrogen in the LEM by controlling the hydrogen price in the LEM according to (31). It is quite simple to observe that the HSSA would like to set \\mu^H in (31) to a positive value close to zero.","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"The HVs are the only consumers of hydrogen in the LEM, and their trading strategies are quite easy to capture. According to (13)-(20) and (34), the HVs will purchase hydrogen from the LEM as much as they need or the LEM can supply, as long as the hydrogen price in the LEM is lower than that from the HS (\\mu^H > 0 in (31)). Since the HSSA is the unique hydrogen producer in the LEM, it is capable of settling the traded amount of hydrogen in the LEM by controlling the hydrogen price in the LEM according to (31). It is quite simple to observe that the HSSA would like to set \\mu^H in (31) to a positive value close to zero."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":", p y 24) P i,tDGdeal,(r−1) at the price of λL,(r−1)t in the r −1th iteration, then the offering par","equation_id":"(33)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Similarly, for Load j, the bidding parameters are \\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} = \\begin{cases} \\lambda_t^{DS}, & \\text{if } P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} \\in S_{j,t}^{Load1,(r)} \\\\ \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)}, & \\text{if } P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} \\in S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)} \\end{cases} \\quad (33) where S_{j,t}^{Load1,(r)} = [0, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)} - P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r-1)}], S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)} = [\\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)} - P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r-1)}, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)}]. Also note that \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} \u003c \\lambda_t^{DS}, otherwise the Load would not participate in the r-1th iteration of LEM.","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","quote":"Similarly, for Load j, the bidding parameters are \\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} = \\begin{cases} \\lambda_t^{DS}, & \\text{if } P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} \\in S_{j,t}^{Load1,(r)} \\\\ \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)}, & \\text{if } P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} \\in S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)} \\end{cases} \\quad (33) where S_{j,t}^{Load1,(r)} = [0, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)} - P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r-1)}], S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)} = [\\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)} - P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r-1)}, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)}]. Also note that \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} \u003c \\lambda_t^{DS}, otherwise the Load would not participate in the r-1th iteration of LEM."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":", p y 24) P i,tDGdeal,(r−1) at the price of λL,(r−1)t in the r −1th iteration, then the offering par","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{DS} \\text{ if } P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} \\in S_{j,t}^{Load1,(r)}; \\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} \\text{ if } P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} \\in S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)} (33) where S_{j,t}^{Load1,(r)} = [0, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)} - P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r-1)}], S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)} = [\\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)} - P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r-1)}, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)}]. Also note that \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} \u003c \\lambda_t^{DS}, otherwise the Load would not participate in the r-1th iteration of LEM.","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","quote":"\\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{DS} \\text{ if } P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} \\in S_{j,t}^{Load1,(r)}; \\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} \\text{ if } P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} \\in S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)} (33) where S_{j,t}^{Load1,(r)} = [0, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)} - P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r-1)}], S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)} = [\\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)} - P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r-1)}, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)}]. Also note that \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} \u003c \\lambda_t^{DS}, otherwise the Load would not participate in the r-1th iteration of LEM."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":", p y 24) P i,tDGdeal,(r−1) at the price of λL,(r−1)t in the r −1th iteration, then the offering par","equation_id":"(32)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For DG i, if the accepted amount of electricity in the LEM is P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r-1)} at the price of \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} in the r-1th iteration, then the offering parameters in the tth iteration are \\lambda_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} = \\begin{cases} \\lambda_t^{DP}, & \\text{if } P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} \\in S_{i,t}^{DG1,(r)} \\\\ \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)}, & \\text{if } P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} \\in S_{i,t}^{DG2,(r)} \\end{cases} \\quad (32) where S_{i,t}^{DG1,(r)} = [0, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{i,t,s}^{DG} - P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r-1)}], S_{i,t}^{DG2,(r)} = [\\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{i,t,s}^{DG} - P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r-1)}, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{i,t,s}^{DG}]. Note that \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} > \\lambda_t^{DP}, otherwise the DG would not participate in the r-1th iteration of LEM.","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"For DG i, if the accepted amount of electricity in the LEM is P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r-1)} at the price of \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} in the r-1th iteration, then the offering parameters in the tth iteration are \\lambda_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} = \\begin{cases} \\lambda_t^{DP}, & \\text{if } P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} \\in S_{i,t}^{DG1,(r)} \\\\ \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)}, & \\text{if } P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} \\in S_{i,t}^{DG2,(r)} \\end{cases} \\quad (32) where S_{i,t}^{DG1,(r)} = [0, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{i,t,s}^{DG} - P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r-1)}], S_{i,t}^{DG2,(r)} = [\\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{i,t,s}^{DG} - P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r-1)}, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{i,t,s}^{DG}]. Note that \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} > \\lambda_t^{DP}, otherwise the DG would not participate in the r-1th iteration of LEM."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p05-c2r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON POWER SYSTEMS, VOL. 33, NO. 4, JULY 2018 the IV. THE ITERATIVE LOCAL ENERGY MAR","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"As stated in Section II, the LEM clearing method is in an iterative manner. The players adjust their offering/bidding parameters after the LEM is cleared, and then the LEM is cleared again with adjusted parameters and broadcasts the results to players until no adjustment of players' offering/bidding parameters is observed. In each iteration process, the LEM clearing method should result in maximizing social welfare and it should respect the merit order principle.","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R009","quote":"As stated in Section II, the LEM clearing method is in an iterative manner. The players adjust their offering/bidding parameters after the LEM is cleared, and then the LEM is cleared again with adjusted parameters and broadcasts the results to players until no adjustment of players' offering/bidding parameters is observed. In each iteration process, the LEM clearing method should result in maximizing social welfare and it should respect the merit order principle."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e14","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p06-c1r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"XIAO et al.: LOCAL ENERGY MARKET FOR ELECTRICITY AND HYDROGEN According to the iterative clearing me","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"According to the iterative clearing method, which will be described in Section IV-C, the HSSA only participates in the LEM after the LEM is cleared in the absence of the HSSA with \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)} generated. Therefore, the offering/bidding parameters of the HSSA are \\lambda_t^{Aoffer,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)}, if P_t^{Aoffer,(r)} \\in [0, P_t^{ALS,(r)}] (35); \\lambda_t^{Abid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)}, if P_t^{Abid,(r)} \\in [0, P_t^{ALP,(r)}] (36).","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R009","quote":"According to the iterative clearing method, which will be described in Section IV-C, the HSSA only participates in the LEM after the LEM is cleared in the absence of the HSSA with \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)} generated. Therefore, the offering/bidding parameters of the HSSA are \\lambda_t^{Aoffer,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)}, if P_t^{Aoffer,(r)} \\in [0, P_t^{ALS,(r)}] (35); \\lambda_t^{Abid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)}, if P_t^{Abid,(r)} \\in [0, P_t^{ALP,(r)}] (36)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON POWER SYSTEMS, VOL. 33, NO. 4, JULY 2018 r), In contrast, the electricity price","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In contrast, the electricity prices are formed through an iteration process to balance supply and demand. As stated in the Step. 3 of the algorithm, the sequences of proposed bids for each consumer j generated by the algorithm are increasing, while the sequences of proposed offers for each producer i are decreasing. To be specific, in a time slot when the supplier finds out its offering amount is completely accepted, whereas there is still some bidding amount of the consumers left, the supplier will elevate its offering price intending to achieve higher utility. In this case, the price will rise consequently, and then the HSSA may increase its offering amount or reduce its bidding amount. As a result, the total supply increases or the total demand decreases, until the supplier no longer observes the complete acceptance of its offering amount or an increase in its utility. It is similar for the case when the consumer observes its bidding amount is completely accepted, whereas there is still some offering amount of the suppliers left. Moreover, as stated in Section IV-A, in the case where the supply and demand curves fail to intersect, the LEM price will be settled as the price of the last unit of accepted amount of the curve that has a surplus. Therefore, the price varies during the iteration process to balance the supply and demand, and will necessarily converge.","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R009","quote":"In contrast, the electricity prices are formed through an iteration process to balance supply and demand. As stated in the Step. 3 of the algorithm, the sequences of proposed bids for each consumer j generated by the algorithm are increasing, while the sequences of proposed offers for each producer i are decreasing. To be specific, in a time slot when the supplier finds out its offering amount is completely accepted, whereas there is still some bidding amount of the consumers left, the supplier will elevate its offering price intending to achieve higher utility. In this case, the price will rise consequently, and then the HSSA may increase its offering amount or reduce its bidding amount. As a result, the total supply increases or the total demand decreases, until the supplier no longer observes the complete acceptance of its offering amount or an increase in its utility. It is similar for the case when the consumer observes its bidding amount is completely accepted, whereas there is still some offering amount of the suppliers left. Moreover, as stated in Section IV-A, in the case where the supply and demand curves fail to intersect, the LEM price will be settled as the price of the last unit of accepted amount of the curve that has a surplus. Therefore, the price varies during the iteration process to balance the supply and demand, and will necessarily converge."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e08","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p05-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON POWER SYSTEMS, VOL. 33, NO. 4, JULY 2018 the IV. THE ITERATIVE LOCAL ENERGY MAR","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"However, if the supply and demand curves fail to intersect, the LEM price will be settled as the price of the last unit of accepted amount on the curve that has a surplus [34].","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R009","quote":"However, if the supply and demand curves fail to intersect, the LEM price will be settled as the price of the last unit of accepted amount on the curve that has a surplus [34]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e24","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"case, the price will rise consequently, and then the HSSA may ies increase its offering amount or re","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"On the other hand, players have the right to choose to trade with the DisCo or in the LEM, thus prices in the LEM will not exceed those of DisCo, i.e., in the range of \\lambda_t^{DP} and \\lambda_t^{DS}. This attribute introduces caps for the LEM prices.","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R009","quote":"On the other hand, players have the right to choose to trade with the DisCo or in the LEM, thus prices in the LEM will not exceed those of DisCo, i.e., in the range of \\lambda_t^{DP} and \\lambda_t^{DS}. This attribute introduces caps for the LEM prices."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"III. Mathematical Models for Players","anchor_text":"ρA,min ≤ρAt ≤ρA,max (24) P ρA ρA ρA,ini (25) th tT −1 = t0 = P tADP + P tALP ≤uAPt P AE L,max (26) P","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"\\lambda_t^{HL} = \\lambda_t^{HS} - \\mu^H (31). Equation (31) shows the relation between hydrogen price from the HS and in the LEM. According to (13)-(20), it is clear to see that when \\mu^H > 0 in (31), HVs will purchase hydrogen from the HSSA up to the maximum the HSSA can provide.","paper":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","rule_id":"v141-c-R009","quote":"\\lambda_t^{HL} = \\lambda_t^{HS} - \\mu^H (31). Equation (31) shows the relation between hydrogen price from the HS and in the LEM. According to (13)-(20), it is clear to see that when \\mu^H > 0 in (31), HVs will purchase hydrogen from the HSSA up to the maximum the HSSA can provide."}],"candidate_only":true,"classification_subtypes":["heterogeneous_energy_pricing_rules"],"projection_statuses":["composite"],"taxonomy":{"primary_family":"kind-L6-53ad3c9992","secondary_families":[],"stage":"L6","ontological_kind":"heterogeneous_energy_pricing_rules"},"semantic_definition":{},"source_units":[{"unit_id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","paper_id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"pricing.local","source_occurrences":[{"id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","market_meaning":"Local clearing results provide feedback for players to adapt their demand-bid parameters toward maximizing their own utilities. Scope: Demand-bid parameter updates during iterative LEM clearing. Condition: A player updates its demand bid using the preceding cleared results. A completed LEM clearing precedes the subsequent demand-bid parameter adjustment. Scope: Temporal order of demand-bid updates between successive LEM clearings. Condition: An additional bid adjustment is undertaken during the iterative process. On the second segment of a Load's demand-bid schedule, the preceding local clearing price supplies the submitted bidding price. Scope: Load demand-bid schedule in equation (33), using the preceding iteration's LEM electricity price. Condition: The requested quantity belongs to S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)}, the closed interval from scenario-average Load demand in iteration r minus its accepted amount in iteration r-1 through scenario-average Load demand in iteration r. On the second segment of an HV's hydrogen demand-bid schedule, the preceding local hydrogen price supplies the submitted bidding price. Scope: HV hydrogen demand-bid schedule in equation (34), using the preceding iteration's LEM hydrogen price. Condition: The requested quantity belongs to S_{k,t}^{HV2,(r)}, the closed interval from scenario-average total hydrogen purchases in iteration r minus hydrogen purchased in the LEM in iteration r-1 through scenario-average total hydrogen purchases in iteration r. The HSSA uses the LEM price cleared without its participation as the price of its subsequently generated electricity demand bid. Scope: HSSA electricity demand-bid formation after the LEM clearing without the HSSA in the same iteration. Condition: The HSSA's requested electricity quantity lies in the closed interval [0, P_t^{ALP,(r)}] specified in equation (36). A Load reduces its bidding price to seek higher utility when the specified allocation conditions hold; otherwise this adjustment is not made. Scope: Load demand-bid price revision for resubmission during Step 3 of the iterative clearing procedure. Condition: The Load's own bidding amount is fully accepted and positive, while total accepted supply is less than total offered supply, as specified in equations (47)-(48). The electricity-price rise precedes the HSSA's possible reduction of its bidding amount; the reduction is not mandatory. Scope: The HSSA's optional electricity-demand quantity response during iterative supply-demand balancing. Condition: A supplier's offer is completely accepted while some consumer bidding amount remains, the electricity price consequently rises, and the HSSA chooses the described demand-reduction response. Demand submissions communicate bids in price and amount in place of players' preferences and detailed appliance profiles. Scope: Information communicated through participating players' demand bids. Demand-bid parameters should assure the submitting player higher utility in the LEM than in trading with the DisCo/HS. Scope: Demand-bid parameter selection by players choosing to participate in the LEM. Condition: A player elects to submit a demand bid in the LEM rather than rely on trading with the DisCo/HS. Players must ensure that their adjustments introduce no decrease in their own utilities. Scope: Demand-bid adjustments during the iterative LEM procedure. Condition: A participating player adjusts its demand bid. The adjustment in iteration r is to revise the adjustment made in iteration r-1. Scope: Loads' demand-bid adjustments in Step 3, comparing iterations r-1 and r. Condition: The preceding adjustment brings no increase in the Load's utility. The first segment of the Load demand-bid schedule assigns the DisCo electricity selling price as the bidding price. Scope: First segment of the Load electricity demand-bid schedule in equation (33). Condition: The requested quantity belongs to S_{j,t}^{Load1,(r)}, the closed interval from zero through scenario-average Load demand in iteration r minus its accepted amount in iteration r-1. The first segment of the HV hydrogen demand-bid schedule assigns the hydrogen-station price as the bidding price. Scope: First segment of the HV hydrogen demand-bid schedule in equation (34). Condition: The requested quantity belongs to S_{k,t}^{HV1,(r)}, the closed interval from zero through scenario-average total hydrogen purchases in iteration r minus hydrogen purchased in the LEM in iteration r-1.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Demand-bid adjustments during the iterative LEM procedure. | Demand-bid parameter selection by players choosing to participate in the LEM. | Demand-bid parameter updates during iterative LEM clearing. | First segment of the HV hydrogen demand-bid schedule in equation (34). | First segment of the Load electricity demand-bid schedule in equation (33). | HSSA electricity demand-bid formation after the LEM clearing without the HSSA in the same iteration. | HV hydrogen demand-bid schedule in equation (34), using the preceding iteration's LEM hydrogen price. | Information communicated through participating players' demand bids. | Load demand-bid price revision for resubmission during Step 3 of the iterative clearing procedure. | Load demand-bid schedule in equation (33), using the preceding iteration's LEM electricity price. | Loads' demand-bid adjustments in Step 3, comparing iterations r-1 and r. | Temporal order of demand-bid updates between successive LEM clearings. | The HSSA's optional electricity-demand quantity response during iterative supply-demand balancing.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e25"]},"constraint_refs":["47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C003","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C004","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C005","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C007"],"decision_anchor":"bidding.demand","source_rule_sha256":"1647f86538d700837059c307789c7e879d669252d17d688720909513da383d62"},{"id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","market_meaning":"Cleared LEM results provide information used by players to update their offering parameters. Scope: Players' supply-offer updates between iterations of LEM clearing. Condition: Players adjust their offering parameters following a clearing result. LEM clearing precedes the players' subsequent offering-parameter updates. Scope: Post-clearing offering-parameter updates in the iterative procedure; initial submissions are outside this temporal assertion. The HSSA uses the LEM electricity price cleared without the HSSA to generate its supply-offer parameters. Scope: HSSA electricity supply-offer generation between the clearing without HSSA and the clearing with HSSA in an iteration. Condition: The current iteration has produced a cleared LEM price without the HSSA. The resulting rise in the LEM electricity price can be followed by an HSSA response that increases its offered quantity; this response is possible rather than mandatory. Scope: HSSA electricity offered-quantity response in the described surplus-demand adjustment during iterative clearing. Condition: A supplier's offering amount is completely accepted while consumers still have unaccepted bidding quantities; the supplier elevates its offering price and the LEM electricity price rises. Supply-offer parameters should assure the submitting player higher utility in the LEM than in trading with the DisCo/HS. Scope: Supply-offer parameters of players that can choose between LEM participation and trading with the DisCo/HS. Players must ensure that their supply-offer adjustments introduce no decrease in their own utilities. Scope: Players' supply-offer adjustments during the iterative LEM procedure. Condition: A player adjusts its supply offer. Players broadcast their offers instead of their preferences and detailed utilization profiles, while competing on both price and amount. Scope: Information disclosed through supply submissions in the distribution-level LEM.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"HSSA electricity offered-quantity response in the described surplus-demand adjustment during iterative clearing. | HSSA electricity supply-offer generation between the clearing without HSSA and the clearing with HSSA in an iteration. | Information disclosed through supply submissions in the distribution-level LEM. | Players' supply-offer adjustments during the iterative LEM procedure. | Players' supply-offer updates between iterations of LEM clearing. | Post-clearing offering-parameter updates in the iterative procedure; initial submissions are outside this temporal assertion. | Supply-offer parameters of players that can choose between LEM participation and trading with the DisCo/HS.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e25"]},"constraint_refs":["47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C003","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C004","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C008","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C009"],"decision_anchor":"bidding.supply","source_rule_sha256":"d8cd244edae596c208b49132740df1d7feccf0f2fc85f104d0bec3a6f1cc9a66"},{"id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R003::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","market_meaning":"Load demand submissions provide inputs to the first electricity clearing. Scope: Electricity clearing using Load submissions in the first phase of each iteration. Condition: The HSSA is absent from this clearing phase. DG supply submissions provide inputs to the first electricity clearing. Scope: Electricity clearing using DG submissions in the first phase of each iteration. Condition: The HSSA is absent from this clearing phase. Load and HSSA demand submissions provide inputs to the electricity clearing with the HSSA. Scope: Electricity clearing using Load and HSSA demand submissions in the second phase of each iteration. Condition: The HSSA is present in this clearing phase. DG and HSSA supply submissions provide inputs to the electricity clearing with the HSSA. Scope: Electricity clearing using DG and HSSA supply submissions in the second phase of each iteration. Condition: The HSSA is present in this clearing phase. Each Load's submitted bidding quantity bounds its accepted electricity allocation above; the written feasible interval also specifies a strictly positive accepted quantity. Scope: Modeled Load electricity allocations in clearing both without and with the HSSA, using constraint (40). Each DG's submitted offering quantity bounds its accepted electricity allocation above; the written feasible interval also specifies a strictly positive accepted quantity. Scope: Modeled DG electricity allocations in clearing both without and with the HSSA, using constraint (39). The HSSA's submitted bidding quantity bounds its accepted electricity demand above; the written feasible interval also specifies a strictly positive accepted quantity. Scope: The HSSA's accepted electricity demand in the clearing model with the HSSA, constraint (44). Condition: The clearing phase includes the HSSA. The HSSA's submitted offering quantity bounds its accepted electricity supply above; the written feasible interval also specifies a strictly positive accepted quantity. Scope: The HSSA's accepted electricity supply in the clearing model with the HSSA, constraint (43). Condition: The clearing phase includes the HSSA. The LEM operator performs local market clearing. Scope: Market clearing in each iteration of the proposed LEM procedure. Control of the local hydrogen price enables the HSSA to determine the quantity of hydrogen traded in the LEM. Scope: Determination of the quantity of hydrogen traded in the LEM through the hydrogen price under equation (31). Condition: The HSSA is the unique hydrogen producer in the LEM. The LEM clearing method should respect the merit order principle in every iteration. Scope: Each iteration of the proposed LEM clearing procedure. Electricity clearing without the HSSA occurs first, followed by electricity clearing with the HSSA. Scope: The two electricity-clearing phases within each iteration. Total accepted DG electricity supply must equal total accepted Load electricity demand. Scope: Electricity allocations in the clearing model without the HSSA, constraint (38). Condition: The HSSA is absent from this clearing phase. Total accepted DG supply plus accepted HSSA supply must equal total accepted Load demand plus accepted HSSA demand. Scope: Electricity allocations in the clearing model with the HSSA, constraint (42). Condition: The HSSA is present in this clearing phase. The procedure returns to Step 1 to repeat the clearing process. Scope: The continuation decision at Step 4 of the iterative clearing procedure. Condition: Further offering/bidding adjustment is still needed. The iteration terminates and final LEM clearing is performed in the presence of the HSSA. Scope: The termination decision at Step 4 of the iterative clearing procedure. Condition: No further offering/bidding adjustment is needed.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Determination of the quantity of hydrogen traded in the LEM through the hydrogen price under equation (31). | Each iteration of the proposed LEM clearing procedure. | Electricity allocations in the clearing model with the HSSA, constraint (42). | Electricity allocations in the clearing model without the HSSA, constraint (38). | Electricity clearing using DG and HSSA supply submissions in the second phase of each iteration. | Electricity clearing using DG submissions in the first phase of each iteration. | Electricity clearing using Load and HSSA demand submissions in the second phase of each iteration. | Electricity clearing using Load submissions in the first phase of each iteration. | Market clearing in each iteration of the proposed LEM procedure. | Modeled DG electricity allocations in clearing both without and with the HSSA, using constraint (39). | Modeled Load electricity allocations in clearing both without and with the HSSA, using constraint (40). | The HSSA's accepted electricity demand in the clearing model with the HSSA, constraint (44). | The HSSA's accepted electricity supply in the clearing model with the HSSA, constraint (43). | The continuation decision at Step 4 of the iterative clearing procedure. | The termination decision at Step 4 of the iterative clearing procedure. | The two electricity-clearing phases within each iteration.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e22","v141-b-g02-e25"]},"constraint_refs":["47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C010"],"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","source_rule_sha256":"5b4eabcb513b4c8b4405936cab8e94ecc7682875ab559a420d762be3ea642db5"},{"id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R007::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R007","market_meaning":"Load participation is conditional on the iteration's local electricity price being strictly lower than the DisCo selling price. Scope: Electricity LEM; Load participation in iteration r-1 at time slot t. Condition: The LEM electricity price satisfies λ_t^{L,(r-1)} \u003c λ_t^{DS}, the DisCo selling price. Household Loads may choose portfolios of electricity purchases from the DisCo and the LEM according to their own utility function. Scope: Household Loads; electricity purchasing options. HVs may purchase hydrogen from the HS or in the LEM. Scope: HVs; hydrogen purchasing options. The HSSA may purchase electricity from both the DisCo and the LEM. Scope: The HSSA acting as an electricity buyer.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Electricity LEM; Load participation in iteration r-1 at time slot t. | HVs; hydrogen purchasing options. | Household Loads; electricity purchasing options. | The HSSA acting as an electricity buyer.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g02-e12"]},"constraint_refs":["47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C001"],"decision_anchor":"participation.consumer","source_rule_sha256":"126f03a096cf9aa980dfb45675b7a6467e8ee97c8c740351ef5cac9f63387d22"},{"id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","market_meaning":"Submission of electricity offers is a means of LEM participation for renewable DGs and the supplier-capable HSS/HSSA. Scope: Electricity-supply participation of renewable DGs and the HSS/HSSA in the LEM. Submission of an electricity bid is a means of LEM participation for the HSS/HSSA when purchasing electricity. Scope: Electricity-demand submissions by the supplier-capable HSS/HSSA. Condition: The HSSA participates as an electricity buyer. Preliminary local clearing without the HSSA, generating its cleared electricity price, precedes participation of the supplier-capable HSSA in that iteration. Scope: HSS/HSSA participation within iteration r of the proposed LEM procedure. A renewable DG's participation in the r-1th LEM iteration is conditional on the local electricity price exceeding the DisCo purchasing price paid to the DG. Scope: Renewable-DG electricity participation at time t in the r-1th LEM iteration. Condition: \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} > \\lambda_t^{DP}. Supplier-capable players share the stated permission to choose LEM participation or trade with their applicable DisCo/HS alternative. Scope: Venue choice stated for all LEM players, including renewable DGs and the supplier-capable HSS. The HSSA may sell both electricity and hydrogen in the LEM. Scope: HSSA participation as an electricity and hydrogen supplier in the LEM.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Electricity-demand submissions by the supplier-capable HSS/HSSA. | Electricity-supply participation of renewable DGs and the HSS/HSSA in the LEM. | HSS/HSSA participation within iteration r of the proposed LEM procedure. | HSSA participation as an electricity and hydrogen supplier in the LEM. | Renewable-DG electricity participation at time t in the r-1th LEM iteration. | Venue choice stated for all LEM players, including renewable DGs and the supplier-capable HSS.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E02b","v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g03-e001"]},"constraint_refs":["47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C004"],"decision_anchor":"participation.prosumer","source_rule_sha256":"18a906a32f4c2438a6bf4e922baf40311c5a96b1e2b164c9a0d8fd63e7eb3580"},{"id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R009","market_meaning":"The iterative local market clearing process generates electricity prices to balance supply and demand. Scope: Electricity-price formation through iterative LEM clearing. The last accepted unit of the local allocation on the surplus curve supplies the unit price used as the LEM price. Scope: Electricity pricing from accepted local allocations when supply and demand curves do not intersect. Condition: The supply and demand curves fail to intersect. The LEM electricity price is bounded by the DisCo purchasing and selling electricity prices. Scope: Electricity-price bounds in the LEM. The LEM hydrogen price equals the hydrogen-station price minus the parameter µ^H, as specified by equation (31). Scope: Hydrogen pricing in the LEM.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Electricity pricing from accepted local allocations when supply and demand curves do not intersect. | Electricity-price bounds in the LEM. | Electricity-price formation through iterative LEM clearing. | Hydrogen pricing in the LEM.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g02-e08","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e24"]},"constraint_refs":["47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C001","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C002","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C003","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C004"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"c63c718d5941d7d21130f6f592c9076ed9222e70494af459761a112631c3b90c"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"On the second segment of a Load's demand-bid schedule, the preceding local clearing price supplies the submitted bidding price. Scope: Load demand-bid schedule in equation (33), using the preceding iteration's LEM electricity price. Condition: The requested quantity belongs to S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)}, the closed interval from scenario-average Load demand in iteration r minus its accepted amount in iteration r-1 through scenario-average Load demand in iteration r.","expression":"λ_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} = λ_t^{L,(r-1)} if P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} ∈ S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)}, where S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)} = [1/N_s ∑_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)} - P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r-1)}, 1/N_s ∑_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)}].","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":["x_load_bid_price","x_load_bid_quantity"],"parameter_refs":["theta_lambda_L_prev","theta_N_s","theta_load_demand_scenario","theta_load_deal_prev"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e12"],"ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":", p y 24) P i,tDGdeal,(r−1) at the price of λL,(r−1)t in the r −1th iteration, then the offering par","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{DS} \\text{ if } P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} \\in S_{j,t}^{Load1,(r)}; \\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} \\text{ if } P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} \\in S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)} (33) where S_{j,t}^{Load1,(r)} = [0, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)} - P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r-1)}], S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)} = [\\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)} - P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r-1)}, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)}]. Also note that \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} \u003c \\lambda_t^{DS}, otherwise the Load would not participate in the r-1th iteration of LEM."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C004","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"On the second segment of an HV's hydrogen demand-bid schedule, the preceding local hydrogen price supplies the submitted bidding price. Scope: HV hydrogen demand-bid schedule in equation (34), using the preceding iteration's LEM hydrogen price. Condition: The requested quantity belongs to S_{k,t}^{HV2,(r)}, the closed interval from scenario-average total hydrogen purchases in iteration r minus hydrogen purchased in the LEM in iteration r-1 through scenario-average total hydrogen purchases in iteration r.","expression":"λ_{k,t}^{HVbid,(r)} = λ_t^{HL,(r-1)} if Q_{k,t}^{HVbid,(r)} ∈ S_{k,t}^{HV2,(r)}, where S_{k,t}^{HV2,(r)} = [1/N_s ∑_s Q_{k,t,s}^{HVP,(r)} - Q_{k,t}^{HVL,(r-1)}, 1/N_s ∑_s Q_{k,t,s}^{HVP,(r)}].","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":["x_hv_bid_price","x_hv_bid_quantity"],"parameter_refs":["theta_lambda_HL_prev","theta_N_s","theta_HV_total_purchase_scenario","theta_HV_LEM_purchase_prev"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13"],"ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e13","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p05-c2r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"(33) ro- P j,t,sL oad,(r ) −P j,tL oaddeal,(r −1) ],SLj,toad2,(r ) where SLj,toad1,(r ) =[0, N1sThe ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\lambda_{k,t}^{HVbid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{HS} \\text{ if } Q_{k,t}^{HVbid,(r)} \\in S_{k,t}^{HV1,(r)}; \\lambda_{k,t}^{HVbid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{HL,(r-1)} \\text{ if } Q_{k,t}^{HVbid,(r)} \\in S_{k,t}^{HV2,(r)} (34) where S_{k,t}^{HV1,(r)} = [0, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s Q_{k,t,s}^{HVP,(r)} - Q_{k,t}^{HVL,(r-1)}], S_{k,t}^{HV2,(r)} = [\\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s Q_{k,t,s}^{HVP,(r)} - Q_{k,t}^{HVL,(r-1)}, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s Q_{k,t,s}^{HVP,(r)}]."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C005","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The HSSA uses the LEM price cleared without its participation as the price of its subsequently generated electricity demand bid. Scope: HSSA electricity demand-bid formation after the LEM clearing without the HSSA in the same iteration. Condition: The HSSA's requested electricity quantity lies in the closed interval [0, P_t^{ALP,(r)}] specified in equation (36).","expression":"λ_t^{Abid,(r)} = λ_t^{LnA,(r)} if P_t^{Abid,(r)} ∈ [0, P_t^{ALP,(r)}]  (36).","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":["x_hssa_bid_price","x_hssa_bid_quantity"],"parameter_refs":["theta_lambda_LnA","theta_HSSA_LEM_purchase_bound"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e16"],"ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C005","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e14","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p06-c1r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"XIAO et al.: LOCAL ENERGY MARKET FOR ELECTRICITY AND HYDROGEN According to the iterative clearing me","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"According to the iterative clearing method, which will be described in Section IV-C, the HSSA only participates in the LEM after the LEM is cleared in the absence of the HSSA with \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)} generated. Therefore, the offering/bidding parameters of the HSSA are \\lambda_t^{Aoffer,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)}, if P_t^{Aoffer,(r)} \\in [0, P_t^{ALS,(r)}] (35); \\lambda_t^{Abid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)}, if P_t^{Abid,(r)} \\in [0, P_t^{ALP,(r)}] (36)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e16","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"DGs and Loads are zero, the offering/bidding parameters of each DG and Load are acquired based on th","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Step 1: Assume the amounts of electricity accepted by all DGs and Loads are zero, the offering/bidding parameters of each DG and Load are acquired based on the optimization of utility functions. The LEM is firstly cleared in the absence of the HSSA after receiving all offering/bidding parameters from DGs and Loads, because the HSSA will use the cleared LEM price without HSSA to generate offering/bidding parameters, according to (35) and (36). The mathematical models of LEM clearing in the absence of the HSSA are as follows, and the objective is to achieve the maximum value of social welfare, represented as \\max_{\\Gamma^{LM,(r)}} U^{LM,(r)} = \\sum_j \\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r)} - \\sum_i \\lambda_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r)} (37) s.t. \\sum_i P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r)} = \\sum_j P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r)} (38); 0 \u003c P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r)} \\le P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} (39); 0 \u003c P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r)} \\le P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} (40)."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C007","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The electricity-price rise precedes the HSSA's possible reduction of its bidding amount; the reduction is not mandatory. Scope: The HSSA's optional electricity-demand quantity response during iterative supply-demand balancing. Condition: A supplier's offer is completely accepted while some consumer bidding amount remains, the electricity price consequently rises, and the HSSA chooses the described demand-reduction response.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e23"],"ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C007","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON POWER SYSTEMS, VOL. 33, NO. 4, JULY 2018 r), In contrast, the electricity price","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In contrast, the electricity prices are formed through an iteration process to balance supply and demand. As stated in the Step. 3 of the algorithm, the sequences of proposed bids for each consumer j generated by the algorithm are increasing, while the sequences of proposed offers for each producer i are decreasing. To be specific, in a time slot when the supplier finds out its offering amount is completely accepted, whereas there is still some bidding amount of the consumers left, the supplier will elevate its offering price intending to achieve higher utility. In this case, the price will rise consequently, and then the HSSA may increase its offering amount or reduce its bidding amount. As a result, the total supply increases or the total demand decreases, until the supplier no longer observes the complete acceptance of its offering amount or an increase in its utility. It is similar for the case when the consumer observes its bidding amount is completely accepted, whereas there is still some offering amount of the suppliers left. Moreover, as stated in Section IV-A, in the case where the supply and demand curves fail to intersect, the LEM price will be settled as the price of the last unit of accepted amount of the curve that has a surplus. Therefore, the price varies during the iteration process to balance the supply and demand, and will necessarily converge."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The HSSA uses the LEM electricity price cleared without the HSSA to generate its supply-offer parameters. Scope: HSSA electricity supply-offer generation between the clearing without HSSA and the clearing with HSSA in an iteration. Condition: The current iteration has produced a cleared LEM price without the HSSA.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e16"],"ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e16","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"DGs and Loads are zero, the offering/bidding parameters of each DG and Load are acquired based on th","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Step 1: Assume the amounts of electricity accepted by all DGs and Loads are zero, the offering/bidding parameters of each DG and Load are acquired based on the optimization of utility functions. The LEM is firstly cleared in the absence of the HSSA after receiving all offering/bidding parameters from DGs and Loads, because the HSSA will use the cleared LEM price without HSSA to generate offering/bidding parameters, according to (35) and (36). The mathematical models of LEM clearing in the absence of the HSSA are as follows, and the objective is to achieve the maximum value of social welfare, represented as \\max_{\\Gamma^{LM,(r)}} U^{LM,(r)} = \\sum_j \\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r)} - \\sum_i \\lambda_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r)} (37) s.t. \\sum_i P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r)} = \\sum_j P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r)} (38); 0 \u003c P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r)} \\le P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} (39); 0 \u003c P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r)} \\le P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} (40)."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The resulting rise in the LEM electricity price can be followed by an HSSA response that increases its offered quantity; this response is possible rather than mandatory. Scope: HSSA electricity offered-quantity response in the described surplus-demand adjustment during iterative clearing. Condition: A supplier's offering amount is completely accepted while consumers still have unaccepted bidding quantities; the supplier elevates its offering price and the LEM electricity price rises.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e23"],"ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON POWER SYSTEMS, VOL. 33, NO. 4, JULY 2018 r), In contrast, the electricity price","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In contrast, the electricity prices are formed through an iteration process to balance supply and demand. As stated in the Step. 3 of the algorithm, the sequences of proposed bids for each consumer j generated by the algorithm are increasing, while the sequences of proposed offers for each producer i are decreasing. To be specific, in a time slot when the supplier finds out its offering amount is completely accepted, whereas there is still some bidding amount of the consumers left, the supplier will elevate its offering price intending to achieve higher utility. In this case, the price will rise consequently, and then the HSSA may increase its offering amount or reduce its bidding amount. As a result, the total supply increases or the total demand decreases, until the supplier no longer observes the complete acceptance of its offering amount or an increase in its utility. It is similar for the case when the consumer observes its bidding amount is completely accepted, whereas there is still some offering amount of the suppliers left. Moreover, as stated in Section IV-A, in the case where the supply and demand curves fail to intersect, the LEM price will be settled as the price of the last unit of accepted amount of the curve that has a surplus. Therefore, the price varies during the iteration process to balance the supply and demand, and will necessarily converge."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C008","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"For a DG, equation (32) sets the iteration-r offering price to the DisCo purchasing price when the offered quantity lies in S_{i,t}^{DG1,(r)}, and to the previous LEM electricity price when it lies in S_{i,t}^{DG2,(r)}; the source also notes that the previous LEM price exceeds the DisCo purchasing price when the DG participated in the previous LEM iteration.","expression":"\\lambda_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} = \\begin{cases} \\lambda_t^{DP}, & \\text{if } P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} \\in S_{i,t}^{DG1,(r)}, \\\\ \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)}, & \\text{if } P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} \\in S_{i,t}^{DG2,(r)}, \\end{cases} \\quad \\text{where } S_{i,t}^{DG1,(r)} = \\left[0, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{i,t,s}^{DG} - P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r-1)}\\right],\\; S_{i,t}^{DG2,(r)} = \\left[\\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{i,t,s}^{DG} - P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r-1)}, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{i,t,s}^{DG}\\right], \\text{ with source condition } \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} > \\lambda_t^{DP} \\text{ for prior DG LEM participation.}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","pricing.local","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["x_dg_offer_price","x_dg_offer_qty"],"parameter_refs":["theta_disco_purchase_price","theta_prev_lem_price","theta_prev_dg_deal","theta_dg_generation","theta_N_s"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13"],"ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C008","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":", p y 24) P i,tDGdeal,(r−1) at the price of λL,(r−1)t in the r −1th iteration, then the offering par","equation_id":"(32)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For DG i, if the accepted amount of electricity in the LEM is P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r-1)} at the price of \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} in the r-1th iteration, then the offering parameters in the tth iteration are \\lambda_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} = \\begin{cases} \\lambda_t^{DP}, & \\text{if } P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} \\in S_{i,t}^{DG1,(r)} \\\\ \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)}, & \\text{if } P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} \\in S_{i,t}^{DG2,(r)} \\end{cases} \\quad (32) where S_{i,t}^{DG1,(r)} = [0, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{i,t,s}^{DG} - P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r-1)}], S_{i,t}^{DG2,(r)} = [\\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{i,t,s}^{DG} - P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r-1)}, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{i,t,s}^{DG}]. Note that \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} > \\lambda_t^{DP}, otherwise the DG would not participate in the r-1th iteration of LEM."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C009","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"For the HSSA, equation (35) sets the iteration-r offering price equal to the LEM electricity price cleared without the HSSA when the HSSA's offered quantity lies in the closed interval from zero through P_t^{ALS,(r)}.","expression":"\\lambda_t^{Aoffer,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)} \\quad \\text{if } P_t^{Aoffer,(r)} \\in [0, P_t^{ALS,(r)}].","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":["x_hssa_offer_price","x_hssa_offer_qty","x_hssa_lem_sale_qty"],"parameter_refs":["theta_lnA_price"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e16"],"ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C009","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e14","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p06-c1r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"XIAO et al.: LOCAL ENERGY MARKET FOR ELECTRICITY AND HYDROGEN According to the iterative clearing me","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"According to the iterative clearing method, which will be described in Section IV-C, the HSSA only participates in the LEM after the LEM is cleared in the absence of the HSSA with \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)} generated. Therefore, the offering/bidding parameters of the HSSA are \\lambda_t^{Aoffer,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)}, if P_t^{Aoffer,(r)} \\in [0, P_t^{ALS,(r)}] (35); \\lambda_t^{Abid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)}, if P_t^{Abid,(r)} \\in [0, P_t^{ALP,(r)}] (36)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e16","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"DGs and Loads are zero, the offering/bidding parameters of each DG and Load are acquired based on th","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Step 1: Assume the amounts of electricity accepted by all DGs and Loads are zero, the offering/bidding parameters of each DG and Load are acquired based on the optimization of utility functions. The LEM is firstly cleared in the absence of the HSSA after receiving all offering/bidding parameters from DGs and Loads, because the HSSA will use the cleared LEM price without HSSA to generate offering/bidding parameters, according to (35) and (36). The mathematical models of LEM clearing in the absence of the HSSA are as follows, and the objective is to achieve the maximum value of social welfare, represented as \\max_{\\Gamma^{LM,(r)}} U^{LM,(r)} = \\sum_j \\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r)} - \\sum_i \\lambda_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r)} (37) s.t. \\sum_i P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r)} = \\sum_j P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r)} (38); 0 \u003c P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r)} \\le P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} (39); 0 \u003c P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r)} \\le P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} (40)."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C010","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Control of the local hydrogen price enables the HSSA to determine the quantity of hydrogen traded in the LEM. Scope: Determination of the quantity of hydrogen traded in the LEM through the hydrogen price under equation (31). Condition: The HSSA is the unique hydrogen producer in the LEM.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15"],"ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C010","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e15","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"C. The Iterative Clearing Procedure The HVs are the only consumers of hydrogen in the LEM, and their","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The HVs are the only consumers of hydrogen in the LEM, and their trading strategies are quite easy to capture. According to (13)-(20) and (34), the HVs will purchase hydrogen from the LEM as much as they need or the LEM can supply, as long as the hydrogen price in the LEM is lower than that from the HS (\\mu^H > 0 in (31)). Since the HSSA is the unique hydrogen producer in the LEM, it is capable of settling the traded amount of hydrogen in the LEM by controlling the hydrogen price in the LEM according to (31). It is quite simple to observe that the HSSA would like to set \\mu^H in (31) to a positive value close to zero."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R007-C001","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Load participation is conditional on the iteration's local electricity price being strictly lower than the DisCo selling price. Scope: Electricity LEM; Load participation in iteration r-1 at time slot t. Condition: The LEM electricity price satisfies λ_t^{L,(r-1)} \u003c λ_t^{DS}, the DisCo selling price.","expression":"\\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} \u003c \\lambda_t^{DS}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R007-theta-lambda-L-prev","v141-c-R007-theta-lambda-DS"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g02-e12"],"ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R007::v141-c-R007-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R007","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":", p y 24) P i,tDGdeal,(r−1) at the price of λL,(r−1)t in the r −1th iteration, then the offering par","equation_id":"(33)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Similarly, for Load j, the bidding parameters are \\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} = \\begin{cases} \\lambda_t^{DS}, & \\text{if } P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} \\in S_{j,t}^{Load1,(r)} \\\\ \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)}, & \\text{if } P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} \\in S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)} \\end{cases} \\quad (33) where S_{j,t}^{Load1,(r)} = [0, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)} - P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r-1)}], S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)} = [\\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)} - P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r-1)}, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)}]. Also note that \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} \u003c \\lambda_t^{DS}, otherwise the Load would not participate in the r-1th iteration of LEM."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":", p y 24) P i,tDGdeal,(r−1) at the price of λL,(r−1)t in the r −1th iteration, then the offering par","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{DS} \\text{ if } P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} \\in S_{j,t}^{Load1,(r)}; \\lambda_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} \\text{ if } P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)} \\in S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)} (33) where S_{j,t}^{Load1,(r)} = [0, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)} - P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r-1)}], S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)} = [\\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)} - P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r-1)}, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)}]. Also note that \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} \u003c \\lambda_t^{DS}, otherwise the Load would not participate in the r-1th iteration of LEM."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C004","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"A renewable DG's participation in the r-1th LEM iteration is conditional on the local electricity price exceeding the DisCo purchasing price paid to the DG. Scope: Renewable-DG electricity participation at time t in the r-1th LEM iteration. Condition: \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} > \\lambda_t^{DP}.","expression":"\\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} > \\lambda_t^{DP}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["participation.prosumer","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta_lambda_L_prev","theta_lambda_DP"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13"],"ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":", p y 24) P i,tDGdeal,(r−1) at the price of λL,(r−1)t in the r −1th iteration, then the offering par","equation_id":"(32)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For DG i, if the accepted amount of electricity in the LEM is P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r-1)} at the price of \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} in the r-1th iteration, then the offering parameters in the tth iteration are \\lambda_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} = \\begin{cases} \\lambda_t^{DP}, & \\text{if } P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} \\in S_{i,t}^{DG1,(r)} \\\\ \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)}, & \\text{if } P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)} \\in S_{i,t}^{DG2,(r)} \\end{cases} \\quad (32) where S_{i,t}^{DG1,(r)} = [0, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{i,t,s}^{DG} - P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r-1)}], S_{i,t}^{DG2,(r)} = [\\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{i,t,s}^{DG} - P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r-1)}, \\frac{1}{N_s}\\sum_s P_{i,t,s}^{DG}]. Note that \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)} > \\lambda_t^{DP}, otherwise the DG would not participate in the r-1th iteration of LEM."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The iterative local market clearing process generates electricity prices to balance supply and demand. Scope: Electricity-price formation through iterative LEM clearing.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e07","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e23"],"ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R009","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p05-c2r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON POWER SYSTEMS, VOL. 33, NO. 4, JULY 2018 the IV. THE ITERATIVE LOCAL ENERGY MAR","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"As stated in Section II, the LEM clearing method is in an iterative manner. The players adjust their offering/bidding parameters after the LEM is cleared, and then the LEM is cleared again with adjusted parameters and broadcasts the results to players until no adjustment of players' offering/bidding parameters is observed. In each iteration process, the LEM clearing method should result in maximizing social welfare and it should respect the merit order principle."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e14","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p06-c1r1__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"XIAO et al.: LOCAL ENERGY MARKET FOR ELECTRICITY AND HYDROGEN According to the iterative clearing me","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"According to the iterative clearing method, which will be described in Section IV-C, the HSSA only participates in the LEM after the LEM is cleared in the absence of the HSSA with \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)} generated. Therefore, the offering/bidding parameters of the HSSA are \\lambda_t^{Aoffer,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)}, if P_t^{Aoffer,(r)} \\in [0, P_t^{ALS,(r)}] (35); \\lambda_t^{Abid,(r)} = \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)}, if P_t^{Abid,(r)} \\in [0, P_t^{ALP,(r)}] (36)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON POWER SYSTEMS, VOL. 33, NO. 4, JULY 2018 r), In contrast, the electricity price","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In contrast, the electricity prices are formed through an iteration process to balance supply and demand. As stated in the Step. 3 of the algorithm, the sequences of proposed bids for each consumer j generated by the algorithm are increasing, while the sequences of proposed offers for each producer i are decreasing. To be specific, in a time slot when the supplier finds out its offering amount is completely accepted, whereas there is still some bidding amount of the consumers left, the supplier will elevate its offering price intending to achieve higher utility. In this case, the price will rise consequently, and then the HSSA may increase its offering amount or reduce its bidding amount. As a result, the total supply increases or the total demand decreases, until the supplier no longer observes the complete acceptance of its offering amount or an increase in its utility. It is similar for the case when the consumer observes its bidding amount is completely accepted, whereas there is still some offering amount of the suppliers left. Moreover, as stated in Section IV-A, in the case where the supply and demand curves fail to intersect, the LEM price will be settled as the price of the last unit of accepted amount of the curve that has a surplus. Therefore, the price varies during the iteration process to balance the supply and demand, and will necessarily converge."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The last accepted unit of the local allocation on the surplus curve supplies the unit price used as the LEM price. Scope: Electricity pricing from accepted local allocations when supply and demand curves do not intersect. Condition: The supply and demand curves fail to intersect.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e08"],"ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R009","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e08","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p05-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON POWER SYSTEMS, VOL. 33, NO. 4, JULY 2018 the IV. THE ITERATIVE LOCAL ENERGY MAR","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"However, if the supply and demand curves fail to intersect, the LEM price will be settled as the price of the last unit of accepted amount on the curve that has a surplus [34]."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The LEM electricity price is bounded by the DisCo purchasing and selling electricity prices. Scope: Electricity-price bounds in the LEM.","expression":"\\lambda_t^{DP} \\le \\lambda_t^{L} \\le \\lambda_t^{DS}","formalization_origin":"equivalent_translation","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R009-x-lambda-L"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R009-theta-lambda-DP","v141-c-R009-theta-lambda-DS"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e24"],"ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R009","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e24","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV. Iterative LEM Clearing Method","anchor_text":"case, the price will rise consequently, and then the HSSA may ies increase its offering amount or re","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"On the other hand, players have the right to choose to trade with the DisCo or in the LEM, thus prices in the LEM will not exceed those of DisCo, i.e., in the range of \\lambda_t^{DP} and \\lambda_t^{DS}. This attribute introduces caps for the LEM prices."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C004","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The LEM hydrogen price equals the hydrogen-station price minus the parameter µ^H, as specified by equation (31). Scope: Hydrogen pricing in the LEM.","expression":"\\lambda_t^{HL} = \\lambda_t^{HS} - \\mu^H","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R009-x-lambda-HL"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R009-theta-lambda-HS","v141-c-R009-theta-mu-H"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05"],"ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R009","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-3c8f4fd002-p05-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"III. Mathematical Models for Players","anchor_text":"ρA,min ≤ρAt ≤ρA,max (24) P ρA ρA ρA,ini (25) th tT −1 = t0 = P tADP + P tALP ≤uAPt P AE L,max (26) P","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"\\lambda_t^{HL} = \\lambda_t^{HS} - \\mu^H (31). Equation (31) shows the relation between hydrogen price from the HS and in the LEM. According to (13)-(20), it is clear to see that when \\mu^H > 0 in (31), HVs will purchase hydrogen from the HSSA up to the maximum the HSSA can provide."}]}],"variables":[{"variable_id":"x_load_bid_price","symbol":"λ_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)}","meaning":"Bidding price submitted by Load j for LEM electricity at time slot t in iteration r; the demand-bid price determined by equation (33).","kind":"operational","domain":"Price in €/kWh defined piecewise by the two interval cases in (33); the source gives no separate numeric interval beyond those cases.","unit":"€/kWh","indices":["j","t","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g01-E02"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::x::x_load_bid_price"},{"variable_id":"x_load_bid_quantity","symbol":"P_{j,t}^{Loadbid,(r)}","meaning":"Bidding amount of electricity requested by Load j in the LEM at time t in iteration r.","kind":"operational","domain":"Electricity quantity in kWh tested for membership in S_{j,t}^{Load1,(r)} or S_{j,t}^{Load2,(r)} by (33); the source gives no separate numeric bound beyond those interval definitions.","unit":"kWh","indices":["j","t","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g01-E02"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::x::x_load_bid_quantity"},{"variable_id":"x_hv_bid_price","symbol":"λ_{k,t}^{HVbid,(r)}","meaning":"Bidding price submitted by HV k for LEM hydrogen at time slot t in iteration r; determined by equation (34).","kind":"operational","domain":"Price in €/kg defined piecewise by the two interval cases in (34); the source gives no separate numeric interval beyond those cases.","unit":"€/kg","indices":["k","t","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g01-E02"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::x::x_hv_bid_price"},{"variable_id":"x_hv_bid_quantity","symbol":"Q_{k,t}^{HVbid,(r)}","meaning":"Bidding amount of hydrogen requested by HV k in the LEM at time t in iteration r.","kind":"operational","domain":"Hydrogen quantity in kg tested for membership in S_{k,t}^{HV1,(r)} or S_{k,t}^{HV2,(r)} by (34); the source gives no separate numeric bound beyond those interval definitions.","unit":"kg","indices":["k","t","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g01-E02"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::x::x_hv_bid_quantity"},{"variable_id":"x_hssa_bid_price","symbol":"λ_t^{Abid,(r)}","meaning":"Bidding price of HSSA for electricity in the LEM at time slot t in iteration r; set by equation (36) using the no-HSSA LEM price.","kind":"operational","domain":"Price in €/kWh set conditionally by (36); the source gives no separate numeric range beyond that condition.","unit":"€/kWh","indices":["t","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g01-E02"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::x::x_hssa_bid_price"},{"variable_id":"x_hssa_bid_quantity","symbol":"P_t^{Abid,(r)}","meaning":"Bidding amount of electricity requested by HSSA in the LEM at time slot t in iteration r.","kind":"operational","domain":"Electricity quantity in kWh required by (36) to lie in [0, P_t^{ALP,(r)}]; the source gives no further explicit numeric interval.","unit":"kWh","indices":["t","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g01-E02b"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::x::x_hssa_bid_quantity"},{"variable_id":"x_dg_offer_price","symbol":"\\lambda_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)}","meaning":"Offering price of DG i in the LEM for time t and iteration r; equation (32) assigns it from the DisCo purchasing price or the previous LEM electricity price.","kind":"operational","domain":"Real-valued price in €/kWh; equation (32) assigns it to either \\lambda_t^{DP} or \\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)}. No separate numeric domain is stated in the quoted rule.","unit":"€/kWh","indices":["i","t","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E02"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::x::x_dg_offer_price"},{"variable_id":"x_dg_offer_qty","symbol":"P_{i,t}^{DGoffer,(r)}","meaning":"Offering amount of DG i in the LEM for time t and iteration r; equation (32) conditions the offer-price branch on its interval.","kind":"operational","domain":"Offered quantity in kWh; equation (32) partitions its values into S_{i,t}^{DG1,(r)} and S_{i,t}^{DG2,(r)}, with endpoints defined from average DG generation and the previous accepted DG amount. No separate numeric domain beyond those source intervals is stated.","unit":"kWh","indices":["i","t","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E02"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::x::x_dg_offer_qty"},{"variable_id":"x_hssa_offer_price","symbol":"\\lambda_t^{Aoffer,(r)}","meaning":"Offering price of the HSSA in the LEM for time t and iteration r; equation (35) sets it to the no-HSSA LEM price under the stated quantity condition.","kind":"operational","domain":"Real-valued price in €/kWh; equation (35) assigns it to \\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)} when the offer-quantity condition holds. No separate numeric domain is stated in the quoted rule.","unit":"€/kWh","indices":["t","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g01-E02"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::x::x_hssa_offer_price"},{"variable_id":"x_hssa_offer_qty","symbol":"P_t^{Aoffer,(r)}","meaning":"Offering amount of the HSSA in the LEM for time t and iteration r; equation (35) conditions the offer-price equality on its lying in [0,P_t^{ALS,(r)}].","kind":"operational","domain":"Offered quantity in kWh; equation (35) conditions the offer-price equality on P_t^{Aoffer,(r)} \\in [0,P_t^{ALS,(r)}]. No separate numeric domain is stated.","unit":"kWh","indices":["t","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g01-E02"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::x::x_hssa_offer_qty"},{"variable_id":"x_hssa_lem_sale_qty","symbol":"P_t^{ALS,(r)}","meaning":"Electricity quantity sold in the LEM by the HSSA, used as the upper endpoint of the offer-quantity interval in equation (35); source lists it in the HSSA variable set.","kind":"operational","domain":"Electricity quantity in kWh; source places P_t^{ALS,(r)} in the HSSA variable set and uses it as the upper bound in equation (35). No separate numeric domain is stated in the quoted rule.","unit":"kWh","indices":["t","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g01-E02b"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::x::x_hssa_lem_sale_qty"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R009-x-lambda-L","symbol":"\\lambda_t^{L}","meaning":"LEM electricity price at time slot t.","kind":"operational","domain":"Time-indexed electricity price in the LEM, in €/kWh; the source does not state a separate numeric domain beyond the price bounds in C003.","unit":"€/kWh","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e02","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e24"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R009","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-lambda-L"},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R009-x-lambda-HL","symbol":"\\lambda_t^{HL}","meaning":"LEM hydrogen price at time slot t.","kind":"operational","domain":"Time-indexed hydrogen price in the LEM, in €/kg; its relation to the hydrogen-station price is given by source equation (31).","unit":"€/kg","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e02","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e15"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R009","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-lambda-HL"}],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"theta_lambda_L_prev","symbol":"λ_t^{L,(r-1)}","meaning":"LEM electricity price cleared in the preceding iteration r-1, used as the second-segment Load bid price in equation (33).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"€/kWh","indices":["t","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g01-E14"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::theta::theta_lambda_L_prev"},{"parameter_id":"theta_lambda_HL_prev","symbol":"λ_t^{HL,(r-1)}","meaning":"LEM hydrogen price cleared in the preceding iteration r-1, used as the second-segment HV bid price in equation (34).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"€/kg","indices":["t","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g01-E15"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::theta::theta_lambda_HL_prev"},{"parameter_id":"theta_lambda_LnA","symbol":"λ_t^{LnA,(r)}","meaning":"LEM electricity price cleared without the HSSA in iteration r, used as the HSSA bid price in equation (36).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"€/kWh","indices":["t","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e16"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::theta::theta_lambda_LnA"},{"parameter_id":"theta_N_s","symbol":"N_s","meaning":"Scenario count appearing as the normalization 1/N_s in the scenario-average interval definitions of equations (33)-(34).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e13"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::theta::theta_N_s"},{"parameter_id":"theta_load_demand_scenario","symbol":"P_{j,t,s}^{Load,(r)}","meaning":"Scenario-s Load j electricity demand at time t in iteration r, appearing in the scenario-average interval of equation (33).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kWh","indices":["j","t","s","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g01-E02"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::theta::theta_load_demand_scenario"},{"parameter_id":"theta_load_deal_prev","symbol":"P_{j,t}^{Loaddeal,(r-1)}","meaning":"Accepted electricity amount of Load j in the LEM in iteration r-1, subtracted in the interval definitions of equation (33).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kWh","indices":["j","t","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g01-E02"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::theta::theta_load_deal_prev"},{"parameter_id":"theta_HV_total_purchase_scenario","symbol":"Q_{k,t,s}^{HVP,(r)}","meaning":"Scenario-s total hydrogen purchased by HV k at time t in iteration r, used in the scenario-average interval of equation (34).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kg","indices":["k","t","s","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g01-E02"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::theta::theta_HV_total_purchase_scenario"},{"parameter_id":"theta_HV_LEM_purchase_prev","symbol":"Q_{k,t}^{HVL,(r-1)}","meaning":"Hydrogen purchased by HV k in the LEM at time t in iteration r-1, subtracted in the interval definitions of equation (34).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kg","indices":["k","t","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g01-E02"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::theta::theta_HV_LEM_purchase_prev"},{"parameter_id":"theta_HSSA_LEM_purchase_bound","symbol":"P_t^{ALP,(r)}","meaning":"HSSA electricity purchased in the LEM at time t in iteration r, used as the upper bound on P_t^{Abid,(r)} in equation (36).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kWh","indices":["t","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02b","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g01-E11"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R001","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::theta::theta_HSSA_LEM_purchase_bound"},{"parameter_id":"theta_disco_purchase_price","symbol":"\\lambda_t^{DP}","meaning":"DisCo electricity purchasing price used as the outside-option offer price in the DG supply-offer rule of equation (32).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"€/kWh","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::theta::theta_disco_purchase_price"},{"parameter_id":"theta_prev_lem_price","symbol":"\\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)}","meaning":"LEM electricity price from the previous iteration, used as the second branch of the DG offer-price rule in equation (32).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"€/kWh","indices":["t","r-1"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::theta::theta_prev_lem_price"},{"parameter_id":"theta_prev_dg_deal","symbol":"P_{i,t}^{DGdeal,(r-1)}","meaning":"DG i's accepted LEM electricity amount in the previous iteration, used to define the offered-quantity intervals in equation (32).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kWh","indices":["i","t","r-1"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E02"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::theta::theta_prev_dg_deal"},{"parameter_id":"theta_dg_generation","symbol":"P_{i,t,s}^{DG}","meaning":"DG i's electricity generation in time t and scenario s, used in the average-generation term of the equation (32) intervals.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kWh","indices":["i","t","s"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E07"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::theta::theta_dg_generation"},{"parameter_id":"theta_N_s","symbol":"N_s","meaning":"Normalization factor N_s appearing in the interval definitions of equation (32); the supplied evidence uses N_s but does not explicitly define it in the quoted passage.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::theta::theta_N_s"},{"parameter_id":"theta_lnA_price","symbol":"\\lambda_t^{LnA,(r)}","meaning":"LEM electricity price cleared without the HSSA in iteration r, used by the HSSA to set its offer price in equation (35).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"€/kWh","indices":["t","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g01-E02"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R002::theta::theta_lnA_price"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-lambda-L-prev","symbol":"\\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)}","meaning":"LEM electricity price at time slot t cleared in iteration r-1; the prior local price used in the Load participation condition.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"€/kWh","indices":["t","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g02-e12"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R007","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-lambda-L-prev"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R007-theta-lambda-DS","symbol":"\\lambda_t^{DS}","meaning":"DisCo electricity selling price at time slot t; the outside-option purchase price used as the strict upper threshold in the Load participation condition.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"€/kWh","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g02-e12"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R007","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R007::theta::v141-c-R007-theta-lambda-DS"},{"parameter_id":"theta_lambda_L_prev","symbol":"\\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)}","meaning":"LEM electricity price at time slot t from the preceding iteration r-1, treated as a realized input to the renewable-DG participation condition in C004.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"\\lambda_t^{L,(r-1)}"},"unit":"€/kWh","indices":["t","r"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E02"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R008::theta::theta_lambda_L_prev"},{"parameter_id":"theta_lambda_DP","symbol":"\\lambda_t^{DP}","meaning":"DisCo purchasing price paid to the renewable DG at time slot t; the outside-option price used in the C004 participation condition.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"\\lambda_t^{DP}"},"unit":"€/kWh","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E04b"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R008::theta::theta_lambda_DP"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R009-theta-lambda-HS","symbol":"\\lambda_t^{HS}","meaning":"Hydrogen price from the hydrogen station (outside option) at time slot t.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"€/kg","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e26"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R009","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta-lambda-HS"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R009-theta-mu-H","symbol":"\\mu^H","meaning":"Price difference between the hydrogen-station price λ_t^{HS} and the LEM hydrogen price λ_t^{HL}, in €/kg.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"€/kg","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e15"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R009","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta-mu-H"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R009-theta-lambda-DP","symbol":"\\lambda_t^{DP}","meaning":"DisCo purchasing electricity price at time slot t.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"€/kWh","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e24","v141-b-g02-e27"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R009","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta-lambda-DP"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R009-theta-lambda-DS","symbol":"\\lambda_t^{DS}","meaning":"DisCo selling electricity price at time slot t.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"€/kWh","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e24","v141-b-g02-e27"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R009","declaration_ref":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-theta-lambda-DS"}]}],"source_definitions":[{"unit_id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","stage":"L6","subtype":"heterogeneous_energy_pricing_rules","projection_status":"composite","target_definition":"The electricity unit price is formed by iterative clearing; when the supply and demand curves do not intersect, the price of the last accepted unit on the curve that has a surplus is taken, and λ_t^{DP}≤λ_t^{L}≤λ_t^{DS} is satisfied. The hydrogen unit price is separately formed as λ_t^{HL}=λ_t^{HS}−μ^H and is controlled by the sole hydrogen producer, HSSA.","form_kind":"mathematical","identity_fields":["Object: unit transaction prices of local electricity and hydrogen","Electricity-price relation: the clearing acceptance result forms the unit price; when the curves do not intersect, the price of the last accepted unit on the surplus side is used","Hydrogen-price relation: hydrogen-station reference price minus a price-spread parameter","Output: λ_t^{L} (€/kWh) and λ_t^{HL} (€/kg)"],"variation_fields":["The lower and upper bounds of the electricity price are the DisCo purchase price and the electricity selling price, respectively","Distinguishes the current-round electricity price without HSSA, λ_t^{LnA,(r)}, the previous-round electricity price, and the previous-round hydrogen price","The hydrogen-price reference is λ_t^{HS}; μ^H is a price-spread parameter, and no fixed numerical value is specified","When μ^H>0, HV purchases according to demand and available quantity; the source describes HSSA as tending to select a positive price spread close to zero","Prices may be used for bid formation, participation judgment, and quantity response; each use is retained separately"],"constraint_refs":["47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C003","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C004","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R001::v141-c-R001-C005","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C010","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C001","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C002","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C003","47-electricity_hydrogen_market::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C004"],"paper_id":"47-electricity_hydrogen_market","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"pricing.local","template_code":"DA"}],"source_variants":[],"functional":{"is_child":false,"subdivision_pending":false},"canonical_pointer":"/nodes/236"});
